            "text": "Zhuma Yangzong has spent most of her life in Niru Village, Shangri-La City. Decades ago, Niru, a hidden paradise, remained isolated due to poor transportation and communication. Leaving her homeland was truly unimaginable for herders (牧民) like Zhuma then."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-grammar-fill-2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hubei-wuchang-2026-01-senior-three-january-survey-exam:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "It wasn’t until 1994, when Zhuma Yangzong was in her fifties, that she ventured beyond Niru for the first time to visit her son in Beijing. She walked two days to Shangri-La County town, and then took a three-day bus ride to Kunming, where she boarded a plane and flew to Beijing."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-grammar-fill-3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hubei-wuchang-2026-01-senior-three-january-survey-exam:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "Niru’s transformation began in 2013 when it was recognized as the world’s No.1 eco-village and listed as UNESCO World Heritage Site. Tourists flocked to the village, brought prosperity and improved transportation. With her new-found freedom, Zhuma traveled to Beijing, Tibet, Hainan, Sichuan, and other regions."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-grammar-fill-4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hubei-wuchang-2026-01-senior-three-january-survey-exam:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "At 86, Zhuma fulfilled her dream of visiting the sacred(神圣的) Mount Kailash during her third journey to Tibet. Her family joined her in a pilgrimage, visiting symbolic sites like the Potala Palace and Jokhang Temple. At Chuku Monastery, Zhuma offered a pure white khata, a ceremonial scarf representing her great respect, to the sacred mountain."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-grammar-fill-5",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-hubei-wuchang-2026-01-senior-three-january-survey-exam:grammar-fill:5",
            "text": "As she rested near the sacred mountain, Zhuma reflected on her journey, giving thanks for her improved life, better transportation, and the realization of her long-cherished dream."
          }
